              Cross-compiling NetHack 5.0 for Atari ST/TT/Falcon
              ===================================================

This document covers the Atari-specific bits of cross-compiling
NetHack 5.0 from a Linux host.  See the top-level Cross-compiling
document for the general theory of NetHack's cross-build (HOST
vs TARGET, the five-step build, etc.).

Cross-compiler used:     Thorsten Otto's m68k-atari-mint-gcc
Cross-compiler url:      https://tho-otto.de/crossmint.php
Author of 5.0 support:   Ingo Paschke


Toolchain (quick install)
-------------------------

The companion script sys/atari/install-toolchain.sh fetches the
m68k-atari-mint cross-compiler, mintlib, fdlibm, gemlib, and
E_GEM, and lays them out as a self-contained tree under one
prefix -- same style as /opt/retro68 or /opt/amiga.

    sudo sys/atari/install-toolchain.sh                  # /opt/cross-mint
    ./install-toolchain.sh --prefix=$HOME/cross-mint     # unprivileged
    ./install-toolchain.sh --prefix=/opt/cross-foo --sudo

Resulting layout under $PREFIX:

    $PREFIX/bin/m68k-atari-mint-gcc        (host driver)
    $PREFIX/m68k-atari-mint/bin/*          (binutils target wrappers)
    $PREFIX/lib64/gcc/m68k-atari-mint/15/  (gcc internals)
    $PREFIX/m68k-atari-mint/sys-root/usr/include/  (mintlib + E_GEM)
    $PREFIX/m68k-atari-mint/sys-root/usr/lib/      (libc, libm, libgem, libe_gem)

What each component provides:

  mintlib  C library (libc.a) and headers.  Without this, no C
           program will link.
  fdlibm   Math library (libm.a).  Replaces MiNTLib's libm, which
           has a multiple-definition flaw in 'xcpt' that otherwise
           requires -Wl,--allow-multiple-definition at link time.
  gemlib   AES/VDI bindings (libgem.a, gem.h).
  E_GEM    Higher-level UI toolkit (windows, dialogs, popups,
           sliders, drag-and-drop, XAcc/AV protocols).  Binary
           release as lib_e_gem_*.zip at the EGEM_220 GitHub URL;
           source at the same repo if you want to build it yourself
           (cd EGEM_220/source && make -f makefile.gcc).

Version pins are at the top of the script; override via the
GCC_VER / BINUTILS_VER / MINTLIB_VER / FDLIBM_VER / GEMLIB_VER /
EGEM_VER environment variables if you need a specific release.

Verified with gcc 15.2.0; gcc 14.x also builds NetHack cleanly.


Manual install
--------------

The script is just a wrapper around the steps below.  The host
tarballs put their files under usr/* internally; we want them
under $PREFIX/* directly (self-contained tree), so strip one
leading component on extract.

    sudo mkdir -p /opt/cross-mint
    cd /opt/cross-mint

    # Host tools (gcc + binutils) from https://tho-otto.de/crossmint.php :
    sudo tar xJf gcc-<ver>-bin-linux64.tar.xz      --strip-components=1
    sudo tar xJf binutils-<ver>-bin-linux64.tar.xz --strip-components=1

    # Target libs from https://tho-otto.de/snapshots/{mintlib,fdlibm,gemlib}/
    # -- extract INTO the sysroot subdir, NOT at /:
    sudo mkdir -p m68k-atari-mint/sys-root
    cd m68k-atari-mint/sys-root
    sudo tar xjf <path>/mintlib-<ver>-mint.tar.bz2
    sudo tar xjf <path>/fdlibm-<ver>-mint.tar.bz2
    sudo tar xjf <path>/gemlib-<ver>-mint.tar.bz2

    # E_GEM binary release from
    # https://github.com/ingpaschke/EGEM_220/releases :
    sudo unzip <path>/lib_e_gem_2.2.1.zip -d usr


