Building
--------

On your Linux host, from the top of the NetHack source tree:

    sys/unix/setup.sh sys/unix/hints/linux.500
    make fetch-lua
    make CROSS_TO_ATARI=1 all
    make CROSS_TO_ATARI=1 package

The Atari hint (sys/unix/hints/include/cross-pre2.500) defaults
to TOOLTOP=/opt/cross-mint/bin, matching the install-toolchain.sh
default.  If your toolchain lives elsewhere, override:

    make CROSS_TO_ATARI=1 TOOLTOP=/usr/bin package           # raw tho-otto tarballs at /
    make CROSS_TO_ATARI=1 TOOLTOP=$HOME/cross-mint/bin package

The 'CROSS_TO_ATARI=1' flag activates the Atari hints under
sys/unix/hints/include/cross-*.500, which override TARGET_CC,
TARGET_AR, TARGET_LINK, TARGET_CFLAGS, TARGET_LFLAGS, and the
source/object lists.  The build produces:

    targets/atari/nethack.prg       Atari 68000 m68k-atari-mint
                                    GEM application
    targets/atari/NH500ST.ZIP       Packaged self-contained game
                                    directory (~3 MB) ready to
                                    unzip on the Atari side.

ZIP contents are documented in sys/atari/README.tos.


Notes
-----

  - The host-side tool bmp2img_host is built with the host's native
    compiler and run on the host to convert nhtiles.bmp into the
    three IMG tile sheets (NH16.IMG, NH32.IMG, NH2.IMG) that ship in
    the package.

  - For playing the game and end-user configuration, see
    sys/atari/README.tos.
